{"url": "https://asia.nikkei.com/business/transportation/railway-development-drives-tokyo-s-growth-as-world-s-largest-metro-area", "ok": true, "title": "Railway development drives Tokyo's growth as world's largest metro area - Nikkei Asia", "markdown": "[Transportation](https://asia.nikkei.com/business/transportation)\n\nOutward expansion brings influx from rural regions as Japan's total population declines\n\nPeople head for Tsukuba Station on the TX line during morning rush hour on Oct.1 in Tsukuba, Ibaraki prefecture. (Photo by Daishi Abe)\n\nDAISHI ABE\n\nOctober 13, 2025 17:01 JST\n\nListen\n\nTOKYO -- The continuing development of Tokyo's railway infrastructure is fueling further growth of the capital's sprawling metropolitan area, solidifying its status as the world's largest with 37 million people -- about a third of Japan's total population.\n\n## Read Next\n\n- [![Tokyo's busy Yamanote loop line to go driverless by 2035](https://images.ft.com/v3/image/raw/https%3A%2F%2Fcms-image-bucket-productionv3-ap-northeast-1-a7d2.s3.ap-northeast-1.amazonaws.com%2Fimages%2F4%2F7%2F8%2F1%2F11451874-2-eng-GB%2F33dd6ed12780-photo.JPG?fit=cover&gravity=faces&dpr=2&quality=medium&source=nar-cms&format=auto&width=700&height=394)](https://asia.nikkei.com/business/transportation/tokyo-s-busy-yamanote-loop-line-to-go-driverless-by-2035)\n\t[\n\tTransportation\n\t](https://asia.nikkei.com/business/transportation)\n\t#### [Tokyo's busy Yamanote loop line to go driverless by 2035](https://asia.nikkei.com/business/transportation/tokyo-s-busy-yamanote-loop-line-to-go-driverless-by-2035)\n\n- [\n\tBusiness deals\n\t](https://asia.nikkei.com/business/business-deals)\n\t#### [Japan's Sapporo nears deal with KKR-PAG group to sell real estate business](https://asia.nikkei.com/business/business-deals/japan-s-sapporo-nears-deal-with-kkr-pag-group-to-sell-real-estate-business)\n\t[![Japan's Sapporo nears deal with KKR-PAG group to sell real estate business](https://images.ft.com/v3/image/ra